    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5782A\n\nSPONSOR: BORRELLO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to including Silver Lake\nOutlet within the definition of \"inland waterways\" for the purposes of\nwaterfront revitalization\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo included Silver Lake Outlet within the definition of \"inland water-\nways\" for the purpose of waterfront realization.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Paragraph (a) consists of the state's major inland creeks,\nwith Silver Lake Outlet (in Wyoming).\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill allows Silver Lake Outlet, which is currently excluded, to be\ndefined within \"inland waterways\" just Silver Lake is already included.\nThe county currently cannot apply for funding for the outlet because it\nwas excluded from the definition.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe act shall take effect immediately.\n",
